:true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomReflectable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Hashable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/MutableDirectedGraph-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", and a weight can live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(amortized, like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A hash table from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot pair to position (open addressing with a multiplicative hash, not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":"’s SipHash)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1) expected. A graph built in bulk from sorted edges (a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condensation, a line graph, a named graph) builds that table on its first lookup or mutation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in O(m), so a result that is only traversed never pays for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModule/AdjacencyList/insert(checked:)":{"title":"insert(checked:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inserts "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge"},{"type":"text","text":" only when both endpoints are already vertices; otherwise throws and changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing. O(1) expected."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/insert(checked:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"insert"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"checked"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedEdge"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","t